---
import { href } from '../lib/url.js';
---
<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="page">
    <hr />
    <div class="site-footer__grid">
      <!-- Stated once, here, after the evidence — not in the hero.
           The font finding from case study 01 is deliberately NOT claimed: the
           display face on this site is a high-contrast italic, which contradicts
           it. Claiming all four while breaking one would be worse than claiming
           three. See DESIGN-NOTES.md. -->
      <p class="colophon">
        Two findings from <a href={href('/work/01-signage/')}>case study 01</a> are built
        into this site: contrast over colour accents, and motion kept minimal and
        predictable. Body text is set at 7:1 contrast or better throughout, and there is
        one animation — a fade. The display face is chosen against the third finding,
        knowingly.
      </p>
      <p class="meta site-footer__contact">
        <a href="mailto:elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu">elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu</a><br />
        <span>TODO(elina): LinkedIn / GitHub links</span><br />
        <span>London &amp; Seoul &middot; Cambridge, MA from Aug 2026</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .site-footer { margin-top: var(--space-10); padding-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .site-footer__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .site-footer__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 260px; gap: var(--space-8); }
  }
  .colophon {
    font-size: var(--size-2);
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .site-footer__contact span { color: var(--ink-quiet); }
</style>
